      {
        "number": 10,
        "internalPageId": 10,
        "title": "Language Targets",
        "visibleTexts": [
          "Language Targets",
          "Aspects Examples 1 Ask for directions. Where is the park? / How do I get to the bank? / Is the Caffe across the street? 2 State where a place is. I think the public library is along the main avenue on Jefferson Street’s corner. 3 Explain how to get to a place. You have to take the number 10 bus, get off at the West park, walk 1 block and you find the bank.",
          "When we talk about places, we can consider the following aspects.",
          "TO CONSIDER Prepositions are essential to work with these 3 aspects since they state locations and placement."
        ],
